This project builds on the following open-source work:

open_oura — https://github.com/Th0rgal/open_oura
  Copyright (c) 2026 Thomas Marchand (Th0rgal). MIT License.
  Reverse-engineered Oura ring BLE protocol, link, storage and analysis crates.
  Included as a git submodule (upstream/open_oura, pinned commit
  e57c43ce5fe0cf9a646afa790bda3731be767507) and used by path from core/.
  server/ingest.py reproduces the oura-store SQLite schema and server/event_names.py
  mirrors oura-protocol's event-name table, both from that commit.
  patches/0001-no-uuid-discovery-filter-bluez-2282.patch is a modification of
  open_oura's crates/oura-link/src/ble.rs and is offered under the same MIT terms.

open_health — https://github.com/Th0rgal/open_health
  Copyright (c) 2026 Thomas Marchand (Th0rgal). MIT License.
  core/ (the UniFFI RingSession / BleWriter design) is modelled on its
  crates/oura-core. No code is vendored.

Third-party build tooling (Gradle wrapper, Android Gradle Plugin, Kotlin, UniFFI and
Rust crates listed in core/Cargo.lock) is used under the respective licenses.

